---
description: Package ownership and import direction
alwaysApply: true
---

Place code in the lowest package that owns it:

1. `tinker-chest`: platform-neutral utilities
2. `ui/{common,web,mobile}`: shared and platform UI
3. `apparatus/{common,web,mobile}`: shared and platform application logic
4. `gears/*/{common,web,mobile}`: plugin logic
5. `app-{web,mobile}`: composition and entry points

Higher-numbered layers may import lower-numbered layers, never the reverse. Platform packages may import only their matching platform and common packages:

| Package | Can be imported by |
|---------|-------------------|
| Tinker Chest | UI, Apparatus, Gears, Apps |
| UI Common | UI Web/Mobile, Apparatus, Gears, Apps |
| UI Web | Gear Web, App Web |
| UI Mobile | Gear Mobile, App Mobile |
| Apparatus Common | Apparatus Web/Mobile, Gears, Apps; not UI or Tinker Chest |
| Apparatus Web | Gear Web, App Web |
| Apparatus Mobile | Gear Mobile, App Mobile |

Use package aliases across workspaces and relative imports within a workspace.

Keep reusable logic and state in the lowest package that owns them. 
Share code only when behavior is genuinely platform-neutral; duplicate it rather than create an incorrect abstraction. 
Keep apps focused on composition, wiring, and platform concerns.

Before adding logic, search for existing helpers, hooks, services, or utilities. 
Extend or compose them instead of creating parallel implementations. 
Do not duplicate business logic, validation, transformations, formatting, or data fetching.

## UI Layers

Within each `ui/{common,web,mobile}/src` package, higher layers may import lower layers, never the reverse:

1. `design-system`: tokens and `Option`
2. `chassis`, `motion`
3. `hud`: shape primitives
4. `gizmos`: interactive controls, `color-box`, and `tooltip`
5. `rigs`: `popup`, `dialog`, `tabstrip`, and `menu`
6. `forms`
7. `assemblies`: higher-order composites such as `theme-mode-toggle` and `theme-select`

`design-system` must not import other UI layers. 
See `docs/assets/ui-architecture.svg`; update its `.drawio` source and regenerate the SVG when this architecture changes.
